## 3. How to Set Up an SSRF Listener (Interactsh)
To verify blind SSRF bugs (where the server processes your request but doesn't show the output on the page), you need an external server to listen for incoming connections from the target.

   1. Install Interactsh CLI via Go:
   
   go install -v ://github.com
   
   2. Start the client session:
   
   ~/go/bin/interactsh-client
   
   * It will output a unique lookup domain like c84j72...interactsh.com.
   3. Inject your listener domain: Paste that domain into the target's vulnerable parameter field:
   
   https://target.com
   
   4. Check logs: If the target server is vulnerable, your terminal window will flash with incoming HTTP or DNS request logs coming directly from the target company's corporate server IP address.

